    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 1/1 passing).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event by adding one new, self-contained aspect and touching **zero existing files** \u2014 the lowest-impact option under the cost model.\n\n**New file:** `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/advice/OwnerCreatedEventAdvice.java`\n\n- An `@AfterReturning` aspect on `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(..)`, at `@Order(-1)` (higher precedence than the default-ordered advices) so it runs after `membershipLevel` is populated on the response DTO.\n- Emits, via the `AUDIT` logger, an immutable event modeled as a private `record`:\n  `{\"seq\":N,\"ownerId\":\u2026,\"customerCode\":\u2026,\"membershipLevel\":\u2026,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`\n- `seq` is a class-level `AtomicLong` incremented per create, giving a monotonically increasing integer across creates.\n- The event carries the owner's **current primary identifier** through a single `identifier` field (fed `owner.getCustomerCode()` today). When the customerCode is later unified into the memberId, only that one argument changes and the event automatically carries the memberId instead \u2014 while the JSON key stays `customerCode` per the spec.\n\nThis runs *in addition to* the existing human-readable audit line (both the controller's and `OwnerCreateAuditAdvice`'s lines are untouched).\n\n**Why this keeps structural impact low:** the cost formula's biggest lever is `WMC_other` (surrounding class complexity). By putting the behavior in a brand-new class with a single small method, `WMC_other` is effectively 0 \u2192 clamped to 1, the method's CC is minimal, and the file-count multiplier is just 1 \u2014 rather than growing the complexity-laden controller or the existing audit advice.\n\nVerified: `AcceptanceTest.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` passes and the full suite is green.",
